description:
Big changes to the CSS variables that standardizes them and makes `style_panelset()` more accessible.

```css
.panelset {
   --panel-tab-foreground: currentColor;
   --panel-tab-background: unset;
   --panel-tab-active-foreground: currentColor;
   --panel-tab-active-background: unset;
   --panel-tab-active-border-color: currentColor;
   --panel-tab-hover-foreground: currentColor;
   --panel-tab-hover-background: unset;
   --panel-tab-hover-border-color: currentColor;
   --panel-tab-inactive-opacity: 0.5;
   --panel-tabs-border-bottom: #ddd;
   --panel-tab-font-family: Menlo, Consolas, Monaco, Liberation Mono, Lucida Console, monospace;
}
```

All of the `--panel-tab-` prefixes are removed in the arguments to `style_panelset()`, except for `--panel-tabs-border-bottom` which retains the `tabs-` prefix. I also added a `selector` argument so that the style can be made specific to a certain panelset.

Panelsets tabs now wrap when there are too many tabs.

The documentation now provides panelset templates for R Markdown (html4 flavor) and raw HTML.

Closes #37, #38, #39
